-- title:
--   Flatness over a finite flat algebra with reduced generic fibre
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, and let $K$ be a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure making it a fraction field of $R$. Let $B_1$ be a commutative $R$-algebra which is finite as an $R$-module and flat as an $R$-module, and assume that the ring $K \otimes_R B_1$ is reduced. Let $M$ be an abelian group carrying simultaneously an $R$-module structure, a $K$-module structure and a $B_1$-module structure, such that the $K$-action and the $B_1$-action each restrict along $R$ to the given $R$-action (the two scalar-tower hypotheses), and such that scalars from $K$ and from $B_1$ commute in their action on $M$. The conclusion is that $M$ is flat as a $B_1$-module.
--
--   This is the flatness criterion used when a module over a module-finite flat algebra is known to be a vector space over the fraction field of the base in a compatible way; the generic fibre $K \otimes_R B_1$ being reduced forces it to be semisimple. It is invoked in the proof of the faithful flatness of a quotient of a base-changed Hopf algebra by the ideal generated by $1$ minus an orbit idempotent.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Module_Flat_of_module_fractionRing_of_isReduced_baseChange.lean

